As expected, the suit gives off a very Dark
Knight Returns vibe.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:14.610
He used his Leica M Camera to take the picture
so it’s Black and White.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:19.269
But we know a few more facts, so this video
will be a breakdown of both the Suit and the

00:00:19.269 --> 00:00:20.269
Car.

00:00:20.269 --> 00:00:22.640
If you’re finding me for the first time
I do DC Videos every week.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:25.999
Normally they’d be on Wednesday’s because
of Arrow, but as you can see, Batman waits

00:00:25.999 --> 00:00:28.820
for no one.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:32.760
Be sure to subscribe to get everything and
leave me suggestions for bonus videos.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:33.760
So first thing’s first.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:39.390
This is the suit and the car that they’re
using in Superman VS Batman.

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:43.740
Batman is much older a la Ben Affleck’s
50 something Batman versus Christian Bale’s

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:45.650
30 something version of the character.

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:50.070
The suit itself reinforces the idea that they
adapted Frank Miller’s Dark Knight Returns

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:53.970
arc.

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:58.690
In that story Batman is way more jaded and
the world has gone to shit.

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:04.840
Obviously that’s not totally the case in
the world of the Man of Steel movies.

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:10.159
But Batman in this movie, is not going to
start out best buds with Henry Cavill.

00:01:10.159 --> 00:01:14.810
So he’s bringing out the big guns.

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:18.350
Which is where this much more armored looking
suit and car comes from.

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:22.060
You can’t tell because it’s a black and
white photo, but the raised portions of the

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:23.060
suit are silver.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:25.719
It’s silver plates on black tech fabric.

00:01:25.719 --> 00:01:30.399
So they combined the defensive nature of Christian
Bale’s first suit with the modularity of

00:01:30.399 --> 00:01:31.610
the second suit.

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:36.579
And made it a little shinier.

00:01:36.579 --> 00:01:40.700
Here’s the suit from Frank Miller’s Dark
Knight Returns.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:45.249
It’s really Ben Affleck’s ear pieces that
evoke the look.

00:01:45.249 --> 00:01:47.959
This batman always reminded me of the Frank
Castle Punisher.

00:01:47.959 --> 00:01:50.429
Just beating the crap out of villains.

00:01:50.429 --> 00:01:54.420
Supposedly that’s going to be what the initial
meeting of Batman and Superman is going to

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:56.259
be in the Man of Steel sequel.

00:01:56.259 --> 00:01:59.969
Batman sees what happened to Metropolis in
the wake of General Zod’s battle and armors

00:01:59.969 --> 00:02:02.000
up appropriately.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:05.060
Remember when that first movie came out, there
was a big conversation going on about the

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:08.730
amount of damage Superman and Zod did to Metropolis
during their fight.

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:11.970
It was like watching a little kid stomp through
a LEGO model.

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:14.980
They did hundreds of millions of dollars in
damage.

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:19.560
So if you were the world’s greatest detective
and the most cynical superhero on the planet.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:20.580
What would you do?

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:22.970
You’d probably beef up your arsenal.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:27.310
The Batmobile itself is a lot sleeker than
Christian Bale’s tumblr, which is funny,

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:29.750
because it looks more like a real car.

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:36.170
In the Dark Knight Returns comic, the batmobile
is basically a full on tank.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:38.940
So it’s almost like Zack Snyder went in
the opposite direction.

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:42.630
I think it’s just to be more practical.

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:46.940
He’s going up against Superman, at least
during the first part of the movie.

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:50.010
So a tank wouldn’t really help him that
much, and it’s not fast.

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:51.010
At All.

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:52.470
He needs something smaller and quicker.

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:56.020
I’m really interested to find out what kind
of extra weaponry he’s developed.

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:59.510
They’re not completely throwing away all
the canon from Christopher Nolan’s Dark

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:03.280
Knight Trilogy, but they’re not really addressing
anything from those movies either.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:07.120
I still consider Ben Affleck’s version of
the character to be the logical evolution

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.450
of Christian Bale’s character.

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:11.760
And we can’t forget the influence of Wonder
Woman and Cyborg.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:16.760
The movie is going to be like a World’s
Finest version of Justice League.

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:18.980
Before the actual Justice League movie.

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:23.010
I think it’s going to take most of the movie
for the Trinity to come together, so I’m

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:26.630
really interested to see what their chemistry
is.

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:31.310
If you haven’t read DC Comics New 52 version
of Justice League, they essentially got Wonder

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:35.630
Woman and Superman together as a romantic
couple and even though they work together

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:39.590
now, when they first met, Batman pulled out
some kryptonite the first couple of times

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:40.780
he met Superman.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:45.310
So don’t be surprised if Ben Affleck has
the famous Kryptonite Ring in the movie.

00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:47.680
It would be a pretty sweet shout out to the
comics.

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:53.600
Before the new 52 reboot, historically, Batman
kept a Kryptonite ring in case Superman ever

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.240
went out of control.

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:58.930
They movie might deal with this in a more
practical way, but in the comics Superman

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:02.290
is highly vulnerable to magic and mind control.

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:06.790
So he’s been used by supervillains as a
smashy finger puppet on many occasions.

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:10.980
In this movie that’s not going to be the
case, and right now all we know about Lex

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:13.920
Luthor is that he’ll be a really young tech
billionaire.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:17.720
People are calling it a darker version of
his Mark Zuckerberg character from Social

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:18.720
Network.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:21.260
Take that with a grain of salt, but we’re
finally starting to get a look at the movie.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:28.240
Which is awesome.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:31.630
Regardless of what you think about Zack Snyder’s
movies, he’s always been really good about

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:33.210
giving fans an inside look.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:36.970
I remember back at Comic Con 2008 he brought
the Owl Ship from Watchmen.

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:38.280
It was pretty badass.

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:42.380
They built it like a real ship, so don’t
be surprised if the Batmobile is at Comic

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:43.470
Con this year.

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:47.440
The cool thing about all the versions of the
car are that they actually drive.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:51.740
Adam West’s batmobile was probably the closest
to just being a regular car.

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:57.030
When I was a little kid Michael Keaton’s
batmobile was badass, but the funny thing

00:04:57.030 --> 00:05:02.600
is that I found out it weighed so much that
in real life it couldn’t go fast at all.

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:06.290
That all changed when Christopher Nolan built
the Tumblr and then eventually the Bat Pod

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:07.430
motorcycle.

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:08.490
They actually drove really well.

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:12.770
Those tires were huge, so they didn’t turn
super fast, but the tumblr was meant to be

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:15.810
an uban tank that could withstand a missile
blast.

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:19.290
I guess that the new batmobile has to be able
to withstand a superman, but logically the

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:22.060
only way to do that would be to give a coat
of Kryptonite Paint.

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:27.520
I haven’t see it in the comics but I guess
a Kryptonite field generator would be more

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:28.520
effective.

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:33.050
That’s really where Lex Luthor comes in,
I’m really interested to see how he deals

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:36.050
with Superman using modern day technology.

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:40.210
Zack Snyder has taken a much less comical
approach to the character, so I’m expecting

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:43.380
a more advanced version of Bruce Wayne’s
Secret Projects Department.

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:49.419
But now it’s your turn, let me know what
you think of the new suit and batmobile and

00:05:49.419 --> 00:05:53.320
how you think it’s going to inform the movie.

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:57.500
Batman isn’t the type to make friends easily,
so watching them interact for the first time

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:00.180
is going to be a lot of fun.

